# Bootstrap

Before doing anything else in this repository, read `AGENTS.md` at the
repo root. It is the canonical entry point for all coding agents and
contains the routing table for where to read next.

Do NOT broadly grep `docs/` for orientation — `AGENTS.md` §2 tells you
exactly which files to read for the task at hand.

Do NOT read `docs/neural_iv_surface_project_personal_notes.md` or
`docs/neural_iv_surface_research_methodology_narrative.md` unless the
operator explicitly names them — they are the operator's personal,
gitignored notebooks.

Hard rules and git-hook-enforced gates are listed in `AGENTS.md` §3.
Bending any of them requires an explicit env-var waiver
(`WAIVE_DEPS`, `WAIVE_SCOPE`, `WAIVE_TRAILER`). Never silently override.

Agent-driven commits must carry a `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`
trailer (enforced by the `commit-msg` hook once `bash scripts/install_hooks.sh`
has been run on this clone).
